<title>ISRAEL: Average Israeli wage grew 1.2 percent in 1996.</title>
<headline>Average Israeli wage grew 1.2 percent in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average gross monthly wage in Israel was 5,251 shekels in 1996, a real increase 1.2 percent from 1995, the Central Bureau of Statistics said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In 1995, real wages grew 1.9 percent, the bureau said. Last year's overall growth was led by civil service wages, which grew 4.4 percent, it added.</p>
<p>The bureau said that in fourth-quarter the average was 4.1 percent higher than a year earlier.</p>
<p>It said the number of wage-earners grew 4.6 percent to 2.163 million.</p>
<p>($1 = 3.37 shekels)</p>
<p>- Jerusalem newsroom, 972-2-537-0502</p>
